<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bagan, the capital of the Pagan Kingdom from 1044 to 1287, was the site of over 10,000 Buddhist monuments built mainly between the 11th and 13th centuries. Earthquakes and renovations altered it, and it was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a> in 2019.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagan.jpg" alt="Bagan" width="330" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Corto Maltese 1999 · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagan,_Burma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
